    "difficulty": "medium",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the value of <math alttext=\"cosine upper A\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>A</mi></math> in the triangle shown?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The cosine of an acute angle in a right triangle is defined as the ratio of the length of the leg adjacent to the angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In the triangle shown, the length of the leg adjacent to angle <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"41\"><mn>41</mn></math>, and the length of the hypotenuse is <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn></math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"cosine upper A equals StartFraction 41 Over 42 EndFraction\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>42</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"StartFraction 1 Over cosine upper A EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
