    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The figure shows that triangle <math alttext=\"upper Q upper R upper S\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is a right triangle. Each of the given choices is an expression containing <math alttext=\"sine upper Q\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> or <math alttext=\"cosine upper Q\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>. For an acute angle in a right triangle, the sine of the angle is the length of the opposite leg divided by the length of the hypotenuse, and the cosine of the angle is the length of the adjacent leg divided by the length of the hypotenuse. It follows that <math alttext=\"sine upper Q equals StartFraction upper R upper S Over upper Q upper S EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math alttext=\"cosine upper Q equals StartFraction upper Q upper R Over upper Q upper S EndFraction\"><mi>cos</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math alttext=\"upper Q upper R less than upper R upper S\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math>. It's given in the figure that the length of side <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn></math>. Since only the equation <math alttext=\"sine upper Q equals StartFraction upper R upper S Over upper Q upper S EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> contains <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math>, an expression representing <math alttext=\"upper Q upper S\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math> can be found by substituting <math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"upper R upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> in this equation, which yields <math alttext=\"sine upper Q equals StartFraction 25 Over upper Q upper S EndFraction\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"upper Q upper S\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper Q upper S dot sine upper Q equals 25\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>&middot;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"sine upper Q\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper Q upper S equals StartFraction 25 Over sine upper Q EndFraction\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Therefore, the expression <math alttext=\"StartFraction 25 Over sine upper Q EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> represents the length of <math alttext=\"line segment upper Q upper S\"><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&macr;</mo></mover></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>",
