    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the triangle shown, what is the value of <math alttext=\"sine x degree\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": ".6956, .6957, 16/23",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 16 Over 23 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>16</mn>\n<mn>23</mn>\n</mfrac></math>. In a right triangle, the sine of an acute angle is defined as the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the hypotenuse. In the triangle shown, the length of the side opposite the angle with measure <math alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&deg;</mo></math> is <math alttext=\"16\"><mn>16</mn></math> units and the length of the hypotenuse is <math alttext=\"23\"><mn>23</mn></math> units. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"sine x degree\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&deg;</mo></math> is <math alttext=\"StartFraction 16 Over 23 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>16</mn>\n<mn>23</mn>\n</mfrac></math>. Note that 16/23, .6956, .6957, 0.695, and 0.696 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>",
